==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|flatering}}, {{m|enm|flatrung|pos=gerund}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|flatter|ing}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|flă'tərĭng}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈflætəɹɪŋ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-flattering.ogg|a=US}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[attractive|Attractive]] or [[good-looking]]; that makes one look good.
#: {{syn|en|becoming}}
#: {{ant|en|unbecoming|unflattering}}
#: {{ux|en|The dress really did not look very '''flattering''' on her figure.}}
# [[gratifying|Gratifying]] to one's self-esteem; [[complimentary]].
# {{lb|en|of an image etc.}} That which represents too [[favorably]].

